From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:25:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] test(kanban): the sync watcher fences claims from
 startup, before it holds .sync.lock

Audit t_01a1d839f0aa6622 of PR #2715 (landed 9435baf78d, owner t_01a1d6c4e700958e) found that
replacing gateway/kanban_watchers.py's `loop_expected()` with `pass` survived all 111 existing
tests: none drove the real sync watcher through the startup interval before it holds the host
sync lock and checked that the dispatcher's claims are fenced there.

New tests/gateway/test_kanban_sync_watcher_claim_fence.py runs the real
`_kanban_sync_watcher` against a real contended `.sync.lock` (another holder), pauses it in its
lock-retry wait, and ticks the real dispatcher on a primary board (fake Board lease client):

- before any owner record exists, the tick defers the card with `sync_first_round` and it stays
  ready; the waiting watcher writes no record and is not the lock owner (`_STATE.loop` False);
- once the lock owner's record shows its round at the head, the next tick claims the card while
  the record stays the owner's (waiting loop vs lock owner distinction);
- control: with sync disabled the watcher declares nothing and the tick claims at once.

Proof (scratch HOME/HERMES_HOME, scripts/run_tests.sh, zero skips):
GREEN on main 4711fcfa43: 2 passed. sdlc-review mutants.py, baseline 2 passed, every mutant
killed by the startup test with the control passing:
  M1 loop_expected() -> pass (the audit's exact survivor): first tick claimed ([] , running)
  M2 loop_expected also sets _STATE.loop (waiter treated as lock owner)
  M3 waiter calls loop_started (publishes its own record before the lock)
  M4 loop_expected only after the lock is acquired
Test-only change; production code untouched. Card t_01a1d87d1a960fd1.
